# Sentinel Ultra — Local Tooling

Repo root tooling prepares Harbor packages for upload. Prefer commands over reinventing checks.

## Folders

- `incoming/` — drop downloaded task zips
- `tasks/<name>/` — working Harbor task
- `Task_Ready_To_Submit/` — flat upload zips only

## Preferred command

```bash
python scripts/prepare_task.py incoming/<task>.zip --force
```

Or for an extracted task: `python scripts/prepare_task.py tasks/<name>`

## Agent rules

1. Run `python scripts/sentinel_doctor.py` at session start if tooling may be broken.
2. Never claim submit-ready without prepare/check command output.
3. Auto-fixes never touch tracked source under `environment/repo/`.
4. Instruction/test/oracle rewrites still follow Ultra submitter rules; tooling only gates hygiene + packaging.
5. Do not put `runs/` or AI scaffolding in submission zips.
6. Before zip: fix instruction over-prescription (platform `cdg_sentinel_ultra.prescriptiveness` fails CodeBuild). Follow `sentinel-ultra-zip-ready.mdc`.
